In <m147150.184.2CF4ED91@urz-mail.urz.uni-heidelberg.de> m147150@urz-mail.urz.uni-heidelberg.de (Nullmeier, Markus) writes:
>Does that mean there will be full (suitable to an OSF-independent 
>reimplementation) DCE specifications someday? Rumor has it that
>until today such papers just don't exist.

OSF wants to produce specifications that contain enough detail.  It is
almost impossible to write such a document, however.  For example, NFS is
a very simple protocol, but nobody can properly implement it just from
the spec -- you always have to test against the official source and you
always find bugs or glitches that are not documented.

OSF's resources are not infinite (otherwise I'd ask for a big raise :-).
Our priority is on delivering the best possible source code that we can.
