In article <EgsIQsGSMUYQ894eFB@transarc.com> Erik_Brown@transarc.com writes:
>shaver@egsner.cirr.com (Dave Shaver) writes:
>> I'm trying to locate a pthreads package that runs under AIX.  The goal
>> is to find an existing package that we can buy or buy a source code
>> license for a package and do the port ourselves.

>IBM sells a pthread's package as part of their DCE offering.  I believe
>you can buy just the threading component, which is what it sounds like
>you are interested in.  A local IBM sales rep should have this, or my
>company (Transarc) also sells the DCE on AIX as well.

One thing to be wary of if you use DCE threads, however, is that they
were written based on the Posix P1003.4a Draft 4 proposal.  As the
proposal is now up to draft 8, and quite a few things have changed,
you run the risk of being significantly out of step.

A big change is that after draft 4, all blocking system and library
calls are thread cancellation points; this was optional in draft 4 and
DCE threads do not assume it.

Proceed with caution.

  -- David Wright, Hitachi Computer Products (America), Inc.  Waltham, MA
     wright@hi.com  ::  These are my opinions, not necessarily Hitachi's,
     but you're free to disagree, you poor deluded creature


