Folks,

OSF is planning for DCE 1.1 we are trying to determine what to do with the
"DCE User's Guide and Reference".  We have several concerns about the
User's Guide and Reference:

	It contains the only printed reference pages for commands that
	are invaluable to a systems administrator (e.d., acl_edit).

	It contains reference pages for commands that many users may
	never use (e.g., kdestroy).

	We are reconsidering  the appropriate model for a "DCE User".
	Is there really such a thing?  What standard DCE commands
	do they really use?  What do they really need to know?

We have thought of several options:

	Keep the User's Guide structure as it is, but place copies of the
	reference pages in the Administrator's Reference as well.

	Remove all Reference pages from the user's guide, but continue
	to publish the guide.  Put the pages in the Administrator's
	Reference.  Optionally, rename the Administrator's Reference to
	the "Command Reference".

	Eliminate the User's Guide.  Move useful sections to the Admin
	Guide, Admin Reference, and Intro to DCE as appropriate.
	Optionally, rename the Administrator's Reference to the "Command
	Reference".

We would appreciate your comments on:

	1) What is your role: what do you do with DCE? (Do you do DCE
	   systems development, do you develp applications that used
	   DCE, do you use DFS for file access, etc.

	2) What commands do you use?  How often?

	3) What is your view of the "User Model": what is a DCE User, what
	   does the user need to know THAT OSF, as opposed to our
	   licensees, can tell them?

	4) What is the appropriate place for the reference pages that the
	   User's Guide and Rerference currently contains?

	5) What is the appropriateness of having a User Guide at all?

	6) What is the appropriateness of renaming the Administrator's
	   Reference to the "Command Reference" (assuming it contains
	   all DCE commands?

Some issues that need to be considered include whether the current "user"
community is significantly different from the DCE user community will be
once more DCE applications are in place, and what will those people need
that is different from what the (now largely dveloper?) community needs.
--


				Hal


