	At the October OSF DCE Workshop in Karlsruhe, Germany, there
were a couple of papers presented that discussed RPC and CDS
performance, including both response time and throughput.  These papers
appear in the conference proceedings; see "DCE -- The OSF Distributed
Computing Environment", Alexander Schill, editor.  The book is part of
Springer's Lecture Notes in Computer Science (LNCS) series, number 731.
ISBN 3-540-57306-2 and 0-387-57306-2 (two ISBN's are listed).

	One of the papers in the proceedings compares DCE, ONC, DFN, and
PVM.  For a remote call across a variety of packet sizes they saw an
average data rate of 187KB/sec for DCE and 167KB/sec for Sun ONC.
(Note: this average data rate number is meaningless by itself -- this is
just to give you a flavor of the data presented).  The time for a NULL
RPC was 10.3ms for DCE, 7.3ms for ONC.  The full data, including system
types in the test, is in the paper.  Regards,

