>configuration?  Any help or comments are greatly appreciated.

This sort of configuration works. I tried it several months ago with
HP DCE. As another poster pointed out, DCE now tries to find CDS
servers on the local network via broadcast. If that doesn't work, it
does a "defined cached server" based on the hostname you gave it when
it asked for the hostname of the master CDS server. Older versions of
DCE asked a question like "Can this host broadcast to node X?" If you
get this question, the answer in your case is no.

I vaguely remember having a similar problem when we first got HP DCE
"for real". Your /dev/lan0 device must be set to mode 777. If this
isn't the case, do the chmod and try dce_config all over again.

Of course, chmoding /dev/lan0 to 777 is a security hole. I hope HP can
come up with a better solution in the future.

				greg



